+# Capture accuracy from audio
+
+`evals/README.md` measures the sorter on clean text. This folder measures the path the
+phone really uses: a clip is posted to the running server, Whisper transcribes it, and
+what Whisper heard (not the clean text) goes through the real sorter.
+
+## Files
+
+- `run_audio_eval.py`: the runner. Three steps: `stt`, `sort`, `report`. Standard library
+  only, plus what `evals/run_eval.py` needs for `sort`.
+- `test_audio_eval.py`: 20 tests. The server and the model are stubbed. No network.
+- `results-<speech model>-<voice>-<date>.jsonl`: one row per case with `source` (the
+  text that was spoken), `heard`, `seconds`, and the sorter's `items`.
+- `stt-only-*.jsonl`: the same without the sorting step (second accent, and turbo at int8).
+
+The clips are not in the repository. Make them again with gTTS (below).
+
+## Run
+
+    # 1. clips, in a throwaway virtualenv (gTTS calls Google's translate voice, needs network)
+    python -m venv /tmp/tts && /tmp/tts/bin/pip install gTTS
+    /tmp/tts/bin/python -c "
+    import json
+    from gtts import gTTS
+    for line in open('evals/capture_cases.jsonl'):
+        c = json.loads(line)
+        gTTS(c['transcript'], lang='en', tld='com').save('/tmp/clips/' + c['id'] + '.mp3')"
+
+    # 2. server with the speech model under test
+    CAPTURE_TOKEN=x MODEL_NAME=breeze-asr-25 python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
+
+    # 3. measure
+    python evals/audio/run_audio_eval.py stt --clips /tmp/clips --out r.jsonl --model breeze-asr-25 --voice gtts-en-us
+    GEMINI_API_KEY=... python evals/audio/run_audio_eval.py sort --results r.jsonl --delay 5
+    python evals/audio/run_audio_eval.py report --results r.jsonl
+
+    python -m pytest evals/audio -c /dev/null      # the tests
+
+`stt` posts the raw clip with `Content-Type: application/octet-stream`, as the Shortcut
+does. `sort` makes one request at a time; on a rate limit it waits 60 s and tries again,
+at most 8 times per case; on a daily-quota error it stops and a later run resumes. A case
+the API never answered is reported as unanswered, not as wrong. An empty transcript is
+not sent to the sorter, because `POST /capture` answers "No speech detected" and files
+nothing.
+
+## How the numbers are computed
+
+- **Word error rate**: word-level edit distance (substitutions + deletions + insertions)
+  summed over all clips, divided by the number of source words. Lowercase, punctuation
+  stripped. `raw` compares the words as written. `numbers normalised` first rewrites
+  numbers to one spelling, so `five hundred`, `500` and `0.5k` are equal and `RM85` equals
+  `RM 85`. It does not make `fifty` equal `fifteen`.
+- What still counts as an error although nobody misheard anything: `millimetres` vs
+  `millimeters`, `licence` vs `license`, `Dr` vs `Doctor`, `30 dollars` vs `$30`,
+  `SGD` vs `Singapore dollars`, `twelve fifty` vs `12.50`, `1k` vs `one k`, `Y15` vs
+  `Y-15`. Four cases also carry a deliberate mis-hearing in the source text (for example
+  `ring it`, `bill of leading`); when Whisper writes the correct word that is counted
+  against it. So the rate is an upper reading, not a count of hearing mistakes.
+- **End to end**: `evals/score.py`, unchanged, against the unchanged expected answers.
+  The comparison run on clean text is `evals/results-gemini-3.1-flash-lite-2026-11-12.jsonl`.
+
+## Measured 2026-11-20
+
+Real path: the patched server, `POST /transcribe`, CTranslate2 on CPU (4 virtual cores,
+Xeon 2.1 GHz, no GPU). Sorter: `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, free tier. 59 clips, 655 source
+words, 277 s of audio, median clip 4.1 s.
+
+| Speech model | Voice | Word error rate, raw | numbers normalised | Word-perfect clips | End to end | Seconds per clip, median | Peak memory |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `breeze-asr-25` (default) | gTTS US | 14.2% (93/655) | 9.6% (63/655) | 37/59 | answered 59, correct 52 | 12.4 | 3.4 GB |
+| `large-v3-turbo` | gTTS US | 10.7% (70/655) | 7.5% (49/655) | 38/59 | answered 59, correct 48 | 16.4 | 4.5 GB |
+| `large-v3-turbo`, `COMPUTE_TYPE=int8` | gTTS US | 11.0% (72/655) | 7.9% (52/655) | 37/59 | not run | 10.0 | 2.4 GB |
+| `breeze-asr-25` | gTTS UK | 12.8% (84/655) | 9.5% (62/655) | 37/59 | not run | 12.2 | not measured |
+| `large-v3-turbo` | gTTS UK | 12.8% (84/655) | 9.5% (62/655) | 35/59 | not run | 16.5 | not measured |
+
+Clean text, stored run of 2026-11-12: 57 of 59. Word-perfect is after number
+normalisation. Seconds are wall time for the whole request, file conversion included.
+Peak memory is the server process high-water mark (`VmHWM`) after the 59 clips.
+
+Two things the table hides:
+
+- `large-v3-turbo` ships as float16. On this CPU the server loaded it as float32 (the
+  CTranslate2 log says so); the `compute_type` in the registry entry is not what decides
+  that. `COMPUTE_TYPE=int8` made it faster than the default model and smaller.
+- `breeze-asr-25` reported the language as `zh` for all 59 US-voice clips while writing
+  English. `large-v3-turbo` reported `en` for all 59.
+
+### Malay words
+
+An English voice cannot say Malay. The six cases tagged `manglish` (`both-malay-lori`,
+`multi-manglish-run-on`, `date-lusa-malay`, `amount-malay-words`, `malay-esok-klinik`,
+`malay-lori-note`) are therefore a test of a mispronounced input, not of either model on a
+Malay speaker. Others hold single Malay words (`ringgit`, `sen`, `nasi lemak`, `teh tarik`,
+`roti canai`, `nasi kandar`, `aircond`, `lori`).
+
+| Speech model, US voice | Six Malay cases: word errors | end to end | Other 53: word errors | end to end |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `breeze-asr-25` | 28/66 | 3 of 6 | 35/589 (5.9%) | 49 of 53 |
+| `large-v3-turbo` | 24/66 | 1 of 6 | 25/589 (4.2%) | 47 of 53 |
+
+### Which cases changed against the clean-text run, and why
+
+Six flipped cases whose words were heard right or nearly right (two from the breeze list,
+four from the turbo list) were sent to the sorter three more times with the same heard
+text, to tell a hearing problem from sorter variation. "Repeats" below is that check.
+
+`breeze-asr-25`, 5 cases pass on text and fail on audio:
+
+| Case | Cause | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `multi-manglish-run-on` | hearing | `bayar tol` became `by are tall`; the toll was filed as "Bought lunch" |
+| `amount-malay-words` | hearing | `seratus lima puluh` became `Saratis Lima pulo`; filed 50, not 150 |
+| `malay-lori-note` | hearing | `cakap` became `kakup`; a note became a dated task |
+| `multi-three-kinds` | sorting | words equal but `Dr` vs `Doctor`; repeats: 1 of 3 pass |
+| `date-vague-no-due` | sorting | `aircond` vs `aircon`; repeats: 3 of 3 pass |
+
+`large-v3-turbo`, 9 cases pass on text and fail on audio:
+
+| Case | Cause | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| `multi-manglish-run-on` | hearing | `bayar tol` became `buy our tall`; same wrong filing |
+| `amount-malay-words` | hearing | `seratus` became `Serratis`; filed 350, not 150 |
+| `malay-lori-note` | hearing | `cakap` became `Kakup`; a note became a dated task |
+| `malay-esok-klinik` | hearing | `esok` became `Isak`; due today, not tomorrow |
+| `both-malay-lori` | hearing | `esok` became `isaq`; the task lost its date |
+| `multi-two-dated-tasks` | punctuation | every word right, but `...the loan Friday. Send the signed form` ties Friday to the wrong sentence; repeats: 0 of 3 pass |
+| `quote-motorcycle` | scorer | `Y15` written `Y-15`; the note is right, the keyword check `y15` is not met; repeats: 0 of 3 |
+| `date-year-rollover` | sorting | words equal (`eight` vs `8`); due came back 2026-01-03, a year early; repeats: 1 of 3 pass |
+| `ambig-balance-due` | sorting | words equal; one item came back as two; repeats: 1 of 3 pass |
+
+`multi-five-across-topics` and `ambig-lorry-which-project` fail on text and on audio with
+both models. No case went from fail to pass.
+
+Every flip caused by hearing is on a Malay-tagged clip. On the 53 other clips neither
+model lost a case to a misheard word; turbo lost one to punctuation and one to the
+scorer's keyword check.
+
+### The ten most damaging mis-hearings
+
+Ranked by what ended up filed, not by word count.
+
+1. `bayar seratus lima puluh ringgit` -> `Byar Saratis Lima pulo ringat` (breeze, filed
+   50) and `Bayar Serratis Lima Pulo Ringgit` (turbo, filed 350). A wrong amount on disk.
+2. `eh tadi bayar tol 12 ringgit` -> `A toddy by are tall twelve ring it` (breeze) and
+   `A toddy buy our tall 12 ringgit` (turbo). The toll was filed as lunch.
+3. `boss cakap lori sampai PJ warehouse pukul tiga` -> `Boss kakup lori ...` (both). A
+   report of what the boss said became a task due today.
+4. `esok pagi kena pergi klinik` -> `Isak Pagi Kenna Pergi Clinic` (turbo). "Tomorrow"
+   was lost. Breeze wrote `Esak Pagi` and the sorter still read it as tomorrow.
+5. `esok kena confirm masa dengan dia` -> `isaq kenna confirm masa dengan dia` (turbo).
+   The task lost its date.
+6. `lorry is booked already` -> `Laurie is booked already` (breeze) and `Lori is booked
+   already` (turbo). A vehicle became a person.
+7. `...about the loan Friday send the signed form to HR` -> `...about the loan Friday.
+   Send the signed form to HR.` (turbo). No wrong word; the full stop moved the date.
+8. `Honda RS150 seat height` -> `Honda 150 rupees seat height` (both models, both
+   voices). A currency that was never said. The case still passed.
+9. `teh tarik and roti canai six ringgit fifty sen` -> `... 6 ringgit 50 cent` (breeze).
+   Still passed.
+10. `remind me to actually no forget it` -> `Remind me to actually know forget it`
+    (breeze). Still passed (nothing filed).
+
+The one mis-hearing seen in the live run of 2026-11-12, `collect it this Saturday` heard
+as `Collected this Saturday`, did not come back: both models, both voices, four clips,
+all four heard it right. That run used a different synthetic voice.
+
+## Which model should be the default
+
+Not changed. The evidence does not separate the two models.
+
+- Word errors: turbo lower with the US voice (49 vs 63 of 655), equal with the UK voice
+  (62 vs 62). One voice in favour, one a tie.
+- End to end: breeze 52, turbo 48. Turbo failed six cases that breeze passed and breeze
+  failed two that turbo passed. Of turbo's six, one is the scorer's keyword check and two
+  came back right on some repeats; breeze's two are sorter variation as well. The sorter
+  alone moves a result by a few cases between runs, so 52 against 48 is inside that.
+- Speed and memory on this CPU: turbo as shipped is slower and larger; turbo with
+  `COMPUTE_TYPE=int8` is faster and smaller than breeze, with the same word errors as
+  turbo float32 to within three words.
+- Neither model coped with the Malay clips, and those clips are mispronounced, so they
+  say nothing about a Malay speaker.
+
+What changed: the `large-v3-turbo` registry entry now points at a repository that exists
+(`dropbox-dash/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo`, MIT; the Hugging Face API redirects
+faster-whisper's own alias `mobiuslabsgmbh/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo` to it). It was
+downloaded with `scripts/model-manager.sh download large-v3-turbo` and served all the
+turbo rows above. For an English and Manglish speaker it is worth trying on real
+recordings with `MODEL_NAME=large-v3-turbo COMPUTE_TYPE=int8`. A decision needs the
+speaker's own voice: twenty or so real captures from `transcripts.jsonl`, corrected by
+hand, run through both models.
+
+## Limits. Read before quoting a number.
+
+- **n is 59**, six of them Malay. Nothing here is an error rate. A difference of a few
+  cases or a few words between two rows is not a finding.
+- **The cases were written by a model**, not taken from real recordings.
+- **The voice is synthetic** (gTTS 2.5.4, Google's translate voice, `tld=com` for US and
+  `tld=co.uk` for UK): one steady speaker, no background noise, no phone microphone, no
+  car park. A person will be heard worse than this. Sorting was run for the US voice only.
+- **The English voice mispronounces Malay**, so the Malay rows measure the voice.
+- **One sorting run per model.** The sorter is not deterministic; see the repeats above.
+- **Timing** is one pass on a shared 4-core cloud CPU. A sorting job ran alongside part
+  of the turbo passes (network only). A phone-to-server round trip was not measured.
+- **Not run:** a human voice, a real phone recording, sorting for the UK voice or the int8
+  run, Claude as the sorter, a GPU, the Apple (`ggml`) variant, `breeze-asr-25` with
+  `language=en` forced.
